# DAGmate — SIDECAR environment (dagmate-service.service).
#
# Non-secret sidecar config only. The master seed is NOT here — it's delivered
# to the sidecar as a systemd credential from /etc/dagmate/mnemonic (see the
# unit's LoadCredential= and deploy/README.md). Install this file readable by
# the sidecar user:
#     install -o root -g dagmate-svc -m 0640 service.env /etc/dagmate/service.env
#
# systemd EnvironmentFile parses `KEY=value` literally: no shell expansion, no
# quote stripping. Write values bare — no quotes, no trailing spaces.

# ── network ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# mainnet, or a testnet id like testnet-10. Must match site.env.
DAGMATE_NETWORK_ID=mainnet

# Optional. Unset, the SDK's community resolver picks a public node for this
# network and health-checks it (synced + utxoindex + right network) on every
# connection. Set it only to pin a specific node you trust:
#   DAGMATE_KASPA_WRPC=wss://your-node/kaspa/mainnet/wrpc/borsh
# DAGMATE_KASPA_WRPC=

# Optional. With RAKE_BPS=0 no rake output is ever built, so this is unused in
# practice; set it only if you later enable a rake and want it to land somewhere
# other than the operating address. Read by the sidecar.
# DAGMATE_FEE_ADDRESS=

# ── wiring ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Loopback only; nothing but the site backend (same box) talks to the sidecar.
# DAGMATE_SERVICE_HOST=127.0.0.1
# DAGMATE_SERVICE_PORT=8910
